            <ArticleTitle>Clinical Detection of Hemodynamically Significant Isolated Secundum Atrial Septal Defect.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>261-264.e1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-3476(17)31040-5</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpeds.2017.07.037</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The diagnosis of secundum atrial septal defect often is delayed. For 310 patients with hemodynamically significant secundum atrial septal defect undergoing closure over a 5-year period at a single medical center, this study reviews the symptoms prompting referral, limitations of physical examination and electrocardiography, and basis for initially missing the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
